WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.2 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
From Theory of Change to results framework

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A results framework turns your Theory of Change into a table you can monitor from your pilot.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
A results framework turns your Theory of Change into a table. For each external objective it lists the outcomes and outputs you expect, how you will know, and what must hold true.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
What goes in the table

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:38.241
Results chain: Impact, outcomes and outputs, copied from your pathway for the first year. For example: Output 1.1.1: ten repair sessions run. Outcome 1.1: families repair at home.

6
00:00:38.241 --> 00:00:49.200
Evidence: How you will know each result happened, with data you can actually get. For example: Session sheets for the output; a short follow-up call for the outcome.

7
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:57.937
Assumptions: What must hold true for one level to lead to the next. For example: Families can find affordable spare parts nearby.

8
00:00:57.937 --> 00:01:08.985
Codes: The labels from your strategy that link results to plans and budgets. For example: ESO1, Outcome 1.1, Output 1.1.1, used the same way everywhere.

9
00:01:09.385 --> 00:01:09.985
Why it matters

10
00:01:09.985 --> 00:01:15.289
1. Funders often ask for a logframe in your first application.

11
00:01:15.289 --> 00:01:20.963
2. It shows whether your plan adds up before you spend money.

12
00:01:20.963 --> 00:01:27.267
3. It keeps your pilot focused on results you can monitor.

13
00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:28.267
What it feeds

14
00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:33.941
1. Your indicators: at least one for each result in the table.

15
00:01:33.941 --> 00:01:38.874
2. Your plans and budget, linked through the same codes.

16
00:01:38.874 --> 00:01:45.178
3. Your monitoring and reports: planned versus actual, result by result.

17
00:01:45.578 --> 00:01:46.178
What to avoid

18
00:01:46.178 --> 00:01:52.222
Copying every box of your diagram, not only what you can monitor.

19
00:01:52.222 --> 00:01:57.156
Claiming you will measure impact in your first year.

20
00:01:57.156 --> 00:02:03.459
Skipping the logic check, upwards and across to real evidence.

21
00:02:04.059 --> 00:02:05.859
You build a results framework for one external objective.

22
00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:09.859
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:11.359 --> 00:02:14.459
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
